# Independent authored chapter17 preflight

Read-only review of doc/spec/17-math-html.md and doc/migration/authored/17-math-html.nepld against AGENTS.md, doc/authoring.md, spec16/spec21, current annotated writer and canonical page-set contracts. No tracked source or tests were changed. This is preflight, not canonical cutover approval.

No blocking source-semantic or Ruby finding was identified in the full manual read-through. The draft preserves paragraph order and the technical obligations across all seven sections. Minor added Japanese commas and complete-sentence wording in table cells preserve meaning. Sentences with code/link use explicit construction; ordinary text uses sentence literals. Readings split okurigana and particles from kanji bases. No missing required content or added stronger completion claim was found.

Shape: seven sibling Section nodes; two explicit-header tables (3 columns/3 body rows and 2 columns/8 body rows); one flat three-item references list followed by a paragraph in the same Section. No nested lists, parallel, embedded Math/Circuit, image, inline Anchor, or RawCode requires an unsupported profile extension. The code literals are prose/code display, not executable embedded operations. All 21 original Markdown inline code payloads match the 21 Doc InlineCode payloads exactly in order, including the CLI pipe and CSP single quotes. This regex-based literal comparison is appropriate to these simple no-escape payloads but is not production decode or render evidence.

Links: five unchanged external KaTeX URLs, and one relative target18-html-delivery.md without a fragment at draft440. Chapter18 is already registered with logical source doc/spec/18-html-delivery.md. Use markdown-annotated-pages/1 for chapter17; do not rewrite this link to an external GitHub URL or register Markdown as a fake Doc page. Existing single-page host would reject the unresolved requirement by design. No passive host extension is needed. Code-only paths design/markup.json and prose14章 are not additional links.

Content constraints especially retained: KaTeX at generation and not document viewing; independent MathML; no evaluation from rendering; no unapproved arbitrary TeX/HTML; preservation of annotations; typed provider violations vs capability failures; parent Stopped remains Stopped; existing same-request MathML display is not successful operation/save; cumulative fallback budget; bounded maxExpand/maxSize and no false faithful success after clamp; stale response rejection; macro isolation; unobserved Usage not invented; shared preview/export artifact and SaveFinished gating; CSP/asset/doctype/accessibility requirements. Tables keep all eight distinct failure-policy branches.

